    {
      "skill_id": "fr-a1-013",
      "title": "Demonstratives: ce, cet, cette, ces",
      "explanation": "To point to a person or thing, French uses a demonstrative that agrees with the noun. This or that: ce (masculine), cet (masculine before a vowel or a silent h), cette (feminine). These or those: ces (plural, both genders). Examples: ce livre, cet ami, cette maison, ces enfants. Context shows whether ce means this or that.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "fr": "Ce livre est intéressant.",
          "en": "This book is interesting."
        },
        {
          "fr": "Cette femme travaille ici.",
          "en": "This woman works here."
        },
        {
          "fr": "Ces enfants jouent.",
          "en": "These children are playing."
        }
      ],
