    {
      "skill_id": "fr-a1-015",
      "title": "Place prepositions",
      "explanation": "Frequent place prepositions are à (at, to), dans (in), sur (on), sous (under), devant (in front of), derrière (behind), entre (between) and chez (at the home or business of a person). They are followed directly by the noun and its article: sur la table, dans le jardin, devant la porte. Do not add de after devant or derrière. À joins the articles le and les into one word: à + le becomes au, and à + les becomes aux (au marché, aux magasins). Use chez with people: chez Paul.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "fr": "Le chat est sur la table.",
          "en": "The cat is on the table."
        },
        {
          "fr": "Je suis dans le jardin.",
          "en": "I am in the garden."
        },
        {
          "fr": "Nous allons au marché.",
          "en": "We are going to the market."
        }
      ],
      "references": ["FEI-INV"],
